v1.0.55 build 63: finally fix double yellow underline

Root cause: Material's _errorTextStyle fallback in
packages/flutter/lib/src/material/app.dart (line 46-56):

  const TextStyle _errorTextStyle = TextStyle(
    color: Color(0xD0FF0000),
    decoration: TextDecoration.underline,
    decorationColor: Color(0xFFFFFF00),         // PURE YELLOW
    decorationStyle: TextDecorationStyle.double, // DOUBLE LINE
    debugLabel: 'fallback style; consider putting your text in a Material',
  );

When a Text widget has no DefaultTextStyle ancestor in scope, Flutter
falls back to this _errorTextStyle. Our sheet picker's title Text
was inside Container > Column > Row > Expanded > Center > Text, with
no DefaultTextStyle above it. So Flutter painted the double yellow
underline under the title as a debug-indicator warning that there's
no Material/DefaultTextStyle context.

Fix: wrap title in DefaultTextStyle(style: AppTypography.navTitle)
(not .merge — that still inherits decoration). DefaultTextStyle
constructor (not merge) provides a non-merged style that Flutter
honors instead of falling back to the error style.

Also removed unused Material import (was added in build 62 for
Theme.of() workaround, no longer needed).

